2. CLASS (a) — STABLE, CORRECTLY STATIC

  - vos-kernel.md: identity, VSM map, protocols, gates, restrictions —
    stable by design; static is correct.
  - vsm-format-policy: highest-frequency procedure block (applies on every
    .vsm write) — always paid, always used; correct static.
  - RULES.md: EXEMPLAR of the 5.3 pattern — already pointer-compressed
    (4,219 tok -> table, "boot token reduction Nivel 1" 2026-08-12):
    bodies live in canon (hard_rules.vsm), loaded on demand (R5: canon
    over recall). The static-first remedy is already proven in-house.
  - references + skills indexes: two-tier working (index cold, content
    hot) — exactly C3; no content dump in either.

3. CLASS (b) — VOLATILE, VERIFIED NOT COLD-INJECTED

  - current_focus.json: prefix mentions are PATH/protocol only
    (grep -c = 3: boot step, self-dispatch, close rules); content read on
    demand (boot step 3, query_tasks, focus tools). No focus entry has
    ever been in the prefix.
  - state_query / state_onboard / logs: tool surface — read on demand;
    no boot-time state dump exists (opencode.json instructions = RULES.md
    only; references = 739 chars of pointers).
  - Runtime dynamic context (recent_errors, canon drift, focus lists)
    arrives per evaluate call — dynamic-last, not boot injection.
  - Post-compact protocol (ecosystem_refs section 1): RESUMED reminder
    (783) points at INDEXED references instead of retained memory —
    recoverable index > retained tokens (R2 FTS5 idea without injection
    surface). Already implemented; no change needed.

